{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019aVwMX74eUzj2UTpngS3yF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 放弃 'universal depth signal' 叙事，转向 'architecture-conditional depth\n2\t  response'。核心贡献变为：识别 depth signal 存在/崩溃的条件，以及 signal 缺失本身作为生成器 fingerprint 的二阶信号。仍冲\n3\t  EMNLP，定位为 negative/characterization paper。\n4\timagined_experiments:\n5\t- name: feature_ablation_and_trend\n6\t  plan_id: plan_001\n7\t  description: MVP Pythia-only 数据上的特征消融 + 趋势分析 + perplexity 预验证\n8\t  expected_results:\n9\t    full_macro_f1: 0.81\n10\t    reference_only_f1: 0.68\n11\t    surface_only_f1: 0.77\n12\t    ref_vs_surf_bootstrap_p: 0.003\n13\t    h2_features: entropy_mean (slope=-0.42, R²=0.88), ttr (slope=-0.11, R²=0.91),\n14\t      hapax_ratio (slope=-0.14, R²=0.93)\n15\t    h1_features: tail_decay (slope=-0.02, R²=0.15), entropy_std (slope=+0.01, R²=0.08),\n16\t      entropy_max (slope=-0.06, R²=0.31), entropy_min (slope=-0.09, R²=0.42)\n17\t    entropy_min_ambiguous: true\n18\t    median_ppl_by_depth: 13.2, 5.1, 3.2, 2.3, 1.8\n19\t    ppl_depth_spearman: -0.95\n20\t  result_rationale: Pythia-410M reference + Pythia-2.8B generator 是 same-family 最佳条件，即使在\n21\t    worst 档位下初始 MVP 数据仍然能看到 depth signal。问题不在这里暴露——surface features（TTR/hapax）占主导（0.77\n22\t    vs ref-only 0.68）暗示 depth signal 主要来自 vocabulary impoverishment 而非深层 distributional\n23\t    structure。entropy_min 的 R²=0.42 处于模糊地带（不完全 stationary），为后续 cross-family 失败埋下伏笔：这种\n24\t    intermediate behavior 说明 drifting/stationary 分界在不同架构下可能不一致。Reference features\n25\t    弱于 surface 是 worst 档早期信号——如果 dual dynamics 是 robust phenomenon，reference features\n26\t    应至少持平。\n27\t  tables:\n28\t  - name: 'Table: Feature Ablation (5-fold CV, Pythia-2.8B only)'\n29\t    columns:\n30\t    - Feature Set\n31\t    - Macro F1\n32\t    - 95% CI\n33\t    rows:\n34\t    - - Full 7-feature\n35\t      - 0.81\n36\t      - '[0.79, 0.83]'\n37\t    - - Surface only (TTR + hapax)\n38\t      - 0.77\n39\t      - '[0.75, 0.79]'\n40\t    - - Reference only (5 entropy feats)\n41\t      - 0.68\n42\t      - '[0.65, 0.71]'\n43\t    - - entropy_mean alone\n44\t      - 0.64\n45\t      - '[0.61, 0.67]'\n46\t  - name: 'Table: Linear Trend per Feature (depth 0-4)'\n47\t    columns:\n48\t    - Feature\n49\t    - Slope\n50\t    - R²\n51\t    - Classification\n52\t    rows:\n53\t    - - hapax_ratio\n54\t      - -0.14\n55\t      - 0.93\n56\t      - Drifting\n57\t    - - ttr\n58\t      - -0.11\n59\t      - 0.91\n60\t      - Drifting\n61\t    - - entropy_mean\n62\t      - -0.42\n63\t      - 0.88\n64\t      - Drifting\n65\t    - - entropy_min\n66\t      - -0.09\n67\t      - 0.42\n68\t      - Ambiguous\n69\t    - - entropy_max\n70\t      - -0.06\n71\t      - 0.31\n72\t      - Stationary\n73\t    - - tail_decay\n74\t      - -0.02\n75\t      - 0.15\n76\t      - Stationary\n77\t    - - entropy_std\n78\t      - 0.01\n79\t      - 0.08\n80\t      - Stationary\n81\t  figures_description:\n82\t  - 'Fig 1: 7 个特征 mean±std across depth 0-4。hapax/ttr/entropy_mean 呈明显单调下降，entropy_std/tail_decay\n83\t    基本平坦，entropy_min 呈弱下降趋势（R²=0.42），预示跨架构不一致的隐患。'\n84\t  analysis: 'Initial signal looks promising on same-family data but two warning signs:\n85\t    (1) surface features dominate reference features by 9pp, suggesting vocabulary\n86\t    impoverishment is the primary signal carrier, not distributional structure shifts;\n87\t    (2) entropy_min sits in an ambiguous zone. In worst tier these are early indicators\n88\t    that the ''dual dynamics'' framework is architecture-specific — it cleanly separates\n89\t    on Pythia but may not generalize. Proceed to plan_002 but with lowered expectations\n90\t    for cross-family transfer.'\n91\t- name: cross_generator_evaluation\n92\t  plan_id: plan_002\n93\t  description: 5 生成器 (Pythia-2.8B/1B, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-0.6B) LOGO 交叉验证\n94\t  expected_results:\n95\t    total_records: 18200\n96\t    logo_avg_macro_f1_3class: 0.72\n97\t    logo_avg_binary_f1: 0.67\n98\t    logo_per_generator:\n99\t      pythia-2.8b:\n100\t        3class: 0.82\n101\t        binary: 0.78\n102\t      pythia-1b:\n103\t        3class: 0.84\n104\t        binary: 0.8\n105\t      olmo-2-1b:\n106\t        3class: 0.63\n107\t        binary: 0.58\n108\t      qwen3-1.7b:\n109\t        3class: 0.67\n110\t        binary: 0.62\n111\t      qwen3-0.6b:\n112\t        3class: 0.64\n113\t        binary: 0.57\n114\t    per_gen_f1_std: 0.11\n115\t    leave_one_family_out:\n116\t      held_out_pythia: 0.79\n117\t      held_out_olmo: 0.58\n118\t      held_out_qwen: 0.6\n119\t    ablation_full_f1: 0.72\n120\t    ablation_surface_only_f1: 0.7\n121\t    ablation_reference_only_f1: 0.61\n122\t    mcnemar_full_vs_surface_p: 0.12\n123\t    generators_below_060_binary: 2\n124\t    spearman_by_generator:\n125\t      pythia-2.8b:\n126\t        entropy_mean: -0.61\n127\t        ttr: -0.58\n128\t        hapax: -0.63\n129\t      pythia-1b:\n130\t        entropy_mean: -0.55\n131\t        ttr: -0.54\n132\t        hapax: -0.6\n133\t      olmo-2-1b:\n134\t        entropy_mean: -0.22\n135\t        ttr: -0.35\n136\t        hapax: -0.38\n137\t      qwen3-1.7b:\n138\t        entropy_mean: -0.31\n139\t        ttr: -0.4\n140\t        hapax: -0.43\n141\t      qwen3-0.6b:\n142\t        entropy_mean: -0.18\n143\t        ttr: -0.33\n144\t        hapax: -0.36\n145\t    feature_direction_inconsistency: OLMo entropy_mean correlation weakly negative\n146\t      (-0.22) while Pythia strongly negative (-0.61); effect size ratio 2.8x\n147\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档核心假设在此暴露：2+ 新家族 held-out F1 < 0.60。Pythia 家族内 transfer\n148\t    良好（两个 Pythia 模型互相泄露 inductive bias），但 OLMo 和 Qwen 家族 held-out 时 binary F1 掉到 0.57-0.58。原因：(1)\n149\t    OLMo 的 training recipe（Dolma corpus + unique LR schedule）产生不同的 token frequency\n150\t    distribution，导致 Pythia-410M reference model 的 entropy features 对 OLMo 生成文本的 depth\n151\t    drift 不敏感——entropy_mean 的 Spearman 仅 -0.22（vs Pythia -0.61），effect size 缩小 2.8x；(2)\n152\t    Qwen tokenizer 完全不同（byte-level BPE vs Pythia GPT-NeoX tokenizer），surface features（TTR/hapax）的计算基于不同\n153\t    vocabulary space，导致跨家族 surface feature 分布 mismatch；(3) full vs surface-only 差距仅\n154\t    2pp（0.72 vs 0.70），McNemar p=0.12 不显著——7-feature ensemble 在这个场景下不优于简单 surface features，印证\n155\t    ''seven_feat_vs_best_baseline_pp: [0, 2.0]'' 的 worst 预期。per_gen_f1_std = 0.11\n156\t    远高于 ''universal'' 叙事所需的一致性。'\n157\t  tables:\n158\t  - name: 'Table: LOGO Cross-Generator Results'\n159\t    columns:\n160\t    - Held-out Generator\n161\t    - 3-class F1\n162\t    - Binary F1\n163\t    - Family\n164\t    rows:\n165\t    - - Pythia-2.8B\n166\t      - 0.82\n167\t      - 0.78\n168\t      - Pythia\n169\t    - - Pythia-1B\n170\t      - 0.84\n171\t      - 0.8\n172\t      - Pythia\n173\t    - - OLMo-2-1B\n174\t      - 0.63\n175\t      - 0.58\n176\t      - OLMo\n177\t    - - Qwen3-1.7B\n178\t      - 0.67\n179\t      - 0.62\n180\t      - Qwen\n181\t    - - Qwen3-0.6B\n182\t      - 0.64\n183\t      - 0.57\n184\t      - Qwen\n185\t    - - '**Average**'\n186\t      - '**0.72**'\n187\t      - '**0.67**'\n188\t      - —\n189\t  - name: 'Table: Feature Ablation (5-gen LOGO)'\n190\t    columns:\n191\t    - Feature Set\n192\t    - Avg LOGO F1\n193\t    - p vs Full\n194\t    rows:\n195\t    - - Full 7-feature\n196\t      - 0.72\n197\t      - —\n198\t    - - Surface only\n199\t      - 0.7\n200\t      - 0.12 (NS)\n201\t    - - Reference only\n202\t      - 0.61\n203\t      - <0.001\n204\t  - name: 'Table: Spearman ρ (entropy_mean vs depth) by Generator'\n205\t    columns:\n206\t    - Generator\n207\t    - ρ\n208\t    - p-value\n209\t    - Effect interpretation\n210\t    rows:\n211\t    - - Pythia-2.8B\n212\t      - -0.61\n213\t      - <0.001\n214\t      - Strong\n215\t    - - Pythia-1B\n216\t      - -0.55\n217\t      - <0.001\n218\t      - Moderate-Strong\n219\t    - - Qwen3-1.7B\n220\t      - -0.31\n221\t      - <0.001\n222\t      - Weak-Moderate\n223\t    - - Qwen3-0.6B\n224\t      - -0.18\n225\t      - <0.001\n226\t      - Weak\n227\t    - - OLMo-2-1B\n228\t      - -0.22\n229\t      - <0.001\n230\t      - Weak\n231\t  figures_description:\n232\t  - 'Fig 2: Per-generator LOGO F1 bar chart with 95% CI error bars. Clear bimodal\n233\t    pattern: Pythia family (0.78-0.80) vs non-Pythia (0.57-0.62). CI bars for OLMo/Qwen\n234\t    overlap with 0.50 random baseline lower bound.'\n235\t  - 'Fig 3: entropy_mean trend lines (depth 0-4) for each generator. Pythia lines\n236\t    steep and parallel; OLMo nearly flat; Qwen shows weak inconsistent slope. Visual\n237\t    evidence of architecture-conditional response.'\n238\t  analysis: 'Universality claim collapses. The 2-tier pattern (Pythia strong, others\n239\t    weak) indicates depth signal is not an intrinsic property of recursive generation\n240\t    but depends on architecture/training-data alignment with the reference model AND\n241\t    possibly on the generator''s own sampling dynamics. Two interpretations: (A) reference\n242\t    model mismatch — Pythia-410M is a poor scorer for non-Pythia text, inflating entropy\n243\t    baseline and suppressing drift measurement; (B) genuine architecture difference\n244\t    — some models produce more uniform token distributions at every depth, compressing\n245\t    the dynamic range for drift detection. Plan_003 (cross-family reference) will\n246\t    disambiguate. If (A), using OLMo/Qwen reference fixes it; if (B), the signal genuinely\n247\t    doesn''t exist for these families. In worst tier, we expect (B) to dominate. Narrative\n248\t    must pivot to conditional claims.'\n249\t- name: paraphrastic_comparison\n250\t  plan_id: plan_006\n251\t  description: Paraphrasing chains vs continuation chains 直接对比，测试 attractor convergence\n252\t    理论\n253\t  expected_results:\n254\t    paraphrastic_3class_f1: 0.6\n255\t    paraphrastic_binary_f1: 0.53\n256\t    continuation_3class_f1: 0.72\n257\t    continuation_binary_f1: 0.67\n258\t    f1_3class_delta: -0.12\n259\t    spearman_entropy_mean_para: 0.15\n260\t    spearman_entropy_mean_cont: -0.42\n261\t    spearman_ttr_para: 0.31\n262\t    spearman_ttr_cont: -0.48\n263\t    spearman_hapax_para: 0.28\n264\t    spearman_hapax_cont: -0.51\n265\t    cross_transfer_para_to_cont_f1: 0.38\n266\t    cross_transfer_cont_to_para_f1: 0.42\n267\t    depth_retention_para: 0.92\n268\t    depth_retention_cont: 0.83\n269\t    para_attractor_convergence_gen3: true\n270\t    n_paraphrastic: 4800\n271\t    n_continuation: 4600\n272\t  result_rationale: Worst 档下，paraphrastic chains 呈现 attractor convergence 预期行为：entropy_mean\n273\t    Spearman 仅 +0.15（趋于 neutral/轻微 positive，即 paraphrasing 使 perplexity 略微上升后稳定）。但\n274\t    continuation chains 也弱于 expected——在 5-gen pooled data 上 Spearman 仅 -0.42（而非 best\n275\t    档的 -0.65+），因为 non-Pythia generators 拉低了整体 correlation。关键是 sign reversal：paraphrastic\n276\t    正相关 vs continuation 负相关，但 effect size 都不大。Cross-transfer F1 极低（0.38-0.42），说明两种\n277\t    chain 类型的 feature space 几乎不重叠——这在 worst 档是问题而非 feature，因为它意味着 'depth signal' 高度\n278\t    task-specific，不是一个 unified phenomenon。Depth retention 0.92 for para（高于 continuation\n279\t    的 0.83）也 counterintuitive：paraphrasing 保留更多 chains 但 signal 更弱，说明 chain stability\n280\t    ≠ signal strength。Attractor convergence 在 gen-3 后明显——para chains 的 feature 分布停止变化。\n281\t  tables:\n282\t  - name: 'Table: Paraphrastic vs Continuation Depth Signal'\n283\t    columns:\n284\t    - Metric\n285\t    - Paraphrastic\n286\t    - Continuation\n287\t    - Delta\n288\t    rows:\n289\t    - - 3-class LOGO F1\n290\t      - 0.6\n291\t      - 0.72\n292\t      - -0.12\n293\t    - - Binary LOGO F1\n294\t      - 0.53\n295\t      - 0.67\n296\t      - -0.14\n297\t    - - ρ(entropy_mean, depth)\n298\t      - '+0.15'\n299\t      - '-0.42'\n300\t      - sign reversed\n301\t    - - ρ(TTR, depth)\n302\t      - '+0.31'\n303\t      - '-0.48'\n304\t      - sign reversed\n305\t    - - ρ(hapax, depth)\n306\t      - '+0.28'\n307\t      - '-0.51'\n308\t      - sign reversed\n309\t    - - Depth retention (gen4/gen0)\n310\t      - 0.92\n311\t      - 0.83\n312\t      - '+0.09'\n313\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-transfer LOGO F1'\n314\t    columns:\n315\t    - Train on\n316\t    - Test on\n317\t    - F1\n318\t    rows:\n319\t    - - Continuation\n320\t      - Continuation\n321\t      - 0.72\n322\t    - - Paraphrastic\n323\t      - Paraphrastic\n324\t      - 0.6\n325\t    - - Continuation → Para\n326\t      - Paraphrastic\n327\t      - 0.42\n328\t    - - Para → Continuation\n329\t      - Continuation\n330\t      - 0.38\n331\t  figures_description:\n332\t  - 'Fig 4: Parallel feature trajectories (depth 0-4) for para vs cont chains. Continuation\n333\t    lines drift downward (vocabulary impoverishment); paraphrastic lines converge\n334\t    to plateau by gen-3 (attractor behavior). 但两者 effect sizes 都小于 expected。'\n335\t  analysis: 'Sign reversal confirms theoretically expected behavior (paraphrasing\n336\t    → attractor convergence, continuation → monotonic drift), but under worst tier\n337\t    the effect sizes are underwhelming for both types. Paraphrastic binary F1=0.53\n338\t    is near random — essentially unclassifiable beyond gen-0 vs rest. Continuation\n339\t    is better but still weak (0.67 binary). The low cross-transfer (0.38-0.42) means\n340\t    there''s no unified ''depth signal'' that works across chain types — each requires\n341\t    its own model. For EMNLP reframing: this SUPPORTS the ''architecture-conditional''\n342\t    narrative because it shows depth signal properties depend on the specific generation\n343\t    process (paraphrasing vs continuation vs architecture), not just depth itself.\n344\t    The attractor convergence finding is a positive contribution to theory validation\n345\t    even in worst case.'\n346\t- name: finer_grained_ordinal\n347\t  plan_id: plan_009\n348\t  description: 5-class ordinal classification (gen-0 through gen-4) 测试更细粒度深度估计\n349\t  expected_results:\n350\t    5class_macro_f1: 0.38\n351\t    5class_f1_std: 0.04\n352\t    5class_accuracy: 0.42\n353\t    5class_mae: 0.95\n354\t    3class_macro_f1: 0.72\n355\t    delta_5class_vs_3class: -0.34\n356\t    per_class_f1:\n357\t      depth_0: 0.85\n358\t      depth_1: 0.45\n359\t      depth_2: 0.22\n360\t      depth_3: 0.18\n361\t      depth_4: 0.2\n362\t    confusion_concentration: gen2/gen3/gen4 互相混淆，占 confusion matrix off-diagonal 的\n363\t      72%\n364\t    ordinal_methods:\n365\t      CORAL: 0.36\n366\t      frank_hall: 0.39\n367\t      xgboost: 0.38\n368\t    depth_2_3_separability: Cohen's d = 0.08 (entropy_mean), 0.12 (hapax_ratio) —\n369\t      几乎不可分\n370\t    per_family_5class:\n371\t      pythia_held_out: 0.48\n372\t      olmo_held_out: 0.28\n373\t      qwen_held_out: 0.31\n374\t  result_rationale: Worst 档下，5-class 在 pooled 5-gen data 上 macro F1 仅 0.38，接近 5-class\n375\t    random baseline（0.20）但仍显著高于 chance。核心问题：depth 2/3/4 几乎不可分（per-class F1 0.18-0.22）。原因是双重的：(1)\n376\t    depth drift 在多数生成器（OLMo/Qwen）上本身就弱，加上 (2) gen-2 到 gen-4 之间的 feature 增量极小（Cohen's\n377\t    d < 0.12），即使在 Pythia 上也进入 plateau。只有 gen-0 可靠分类（F1=0.85），gen-1 中等（0.45）——这本质上是\n378\t    binary detection（gen-0 vs rest）在 5-class 框架中的残影。OLMo/Qwen held-out 时 5-class F1\n379\t    掉到 0.28-0.31（接近 random），进一步说明 fine-grained 深度估计只在特定架构下可行。Ordinal-specific methods（CORAL/Frank-Hall）无优势，因为\n380\t    underlying signal 本身不存在于 deep depths。3-class（0.72）远优于 5-class（0.38），但 delta =\n381\t    34pp 说明 3-class 的性能也主要来自 gen-0 classification 而非真正的 ordinal discrimination。\n382\t  tables:\n383\t  - name: 'Table: Ordinal Classification Results'\n384\t    columns:\n385\t    - Granularity\n386\t    - Method\n387\t    - Macro F1\n388\t    - MAE\n389\t    rows:\n390\t    - - 3-class\n391\t      - XGBoost\n392\t      - 0.72\n393\t      - 0.31\n394\t    - - 5-class\n395\t      - XGBoost\n396\t      - 0.38\n397\t      - 0.95\n398\t    - - 5-class\n399\t      - CORAL\n400\t      - 0.36\n401\t      - 0.98\n402\t    - - 5-class\n403\t      - Frank-Hall\n404\t      - 0.39\n405\t      - 0.92\n406\t  - name: 'Table: 5-class Per-depth F1'\n407\t    columns:\n408\t    - Depth\n409\t    - F1\n410\t    - Support\n411\t    - Most confused with\n412\t    rows:\n413\t    - - gen-0\n414\t      - 0.85\n415\t      - 4950\n416\t      - gen-1 (10%)\n417\t    - - gen-1\n418\t      - 0.45\n419\t      - 4900\n420\t      - gen-2 (28%)\n421\t    - - gen-2\n422\t      - 0.22\n423\t      - 4600\n424\t      - gen-3 (35%), gen-1 (22%)\n425\t    - - gen-3\n426\t      - 0.18\n427\t      - 4200\n428\t      - gen-2 (33%), gen-4 (30%)\n429\t    - - gen-4\n430\t      - 0.2\n431\t      - 3800\n432\t      - gen-3 (38%), gen-2 (21%)\n433\t  figures_description:\n434\t  - 'Fig 5: 5×5 Confusion matrix heatmap。gen-0 行几乎全在对角线；gen-2/3/4 行呈均匀分布，对角线无明显 peak。直观展示\n435\t    depth > 1 的不可分性。'\n436\t  - 'Fig 6: Feature distributions (violin plots) by depth 0-4, split by generator\n437\t    family。Pythia violins 逐层分离；OLMo/Qwen violins 从 depth-1 开始完全重叠。'\n438\t  analysis: '5-class ordinal is infeasible in worst tier. The signal exists primarily\n439\t    at the gen-0/gen-1 boundary and rapidly degrades. This is actually informative\n440\t    for the reframed paper: it establishes an empirical ceiling on depth resolution\n441\t    (≤3 classes) that''s architecture-dependent. For Pythia-family generators where\n442\t    signal is strong, 4-class might work; for others, even binary (gen-1 vs gen-2+)\n443\t    is near chance. The ''conditions under which depth signal emerges vs collapses''\n444\t    framing gains direct evidence: depth granularity is architecture-conditional,\n445\t    not a universal property of recursive generation. Report as structured negative\n446\t    finding.'\n447\t- name: end_to_end_classifier\n448\t  plan_id: plan_012\n449\t  description: QLoRA fine-tuned Qwen3.5-0.8B 端到端深度分类，对比 handcrafted features\n450\t  expected_results:\n451\t    5class_macro_f1: 0.44\n452\t    5class_f1_std: 0.02\n453\t    3class_macro_f1: 0.76\n454\t    3class_f1_std: 0.01\n455\t    per_class_f1:\n456\t      gen0: 0.95\n457\t      gen1: 0.62\n458\t      gen2: 0.3\n459\t      gen3: 0.22\n460\t      gen4: 0.11\n461\t    vs_xgboost_5class_delta_pp: '+6.0'\n462\t    vs_xgboost_3class_delta_pp: '+4.0'\n463\t    logo_generalization:\n464\t      pythia_held_out: 0.52\n465\t      olmo_held_out: 0.35\n466\t      qwen_held_out: 0.38\n467\t    overfitting_gap: 0.18\n468\t    train_f1: 0.62\n469\t    val_f1: 0.44\n470\t    runtime_hours: 14\n471\t    model: Qwen3-0.6B-Base\n472\t    method: QLoRA rank-16\n473\t  result_rationale: E2E model 在 5-class 上优于 XGBoost（0.44 vs 0.38，+6pp），因为 learned\n474\t    representations 能捕获 handcrafted features 遗漏的 subtle patterns（如 attention pattern\n475\t    shifts、specific n-gram frequency changes）。但绝对性能仍然很差（0.44），且 overfitting 严重（train\n476\t    0.62 vs val 0.44，gap=18pp）——模型学到了 generator-specific artifacts 而非 generalizable\n477\t    depth signal。LOGO generalization 更加灾难性：held-out Pythia F1=0.52，OLMo/Qwen 仅 0.35-0.38。这说明\n478\t    E2E model 学到的不是 'depth signal' 而是 'generator fingerprint + depth 交互'——它在训练集内的\n479\t    generator 上过拟合。3-class（0.76）优于 XGBoost（0.72）但差距不大（+4pp），且同样来自 gen-0 classification。在\n480\t    worst 档下，E2E 的相对优势说明确实有 beyond-handcrafted-features 的信号存在，但这些信号 generator-specific、不泛化，支持\n481\t    'architecture-conditional' reframing。\n482\t  tables:\n483\t  - name: 'Table: E2E vs Handcrafted Features'\n484\t    columns:\n485\t    - Method\n486\t    - 5-class F1\n487\t    - 3-class F1\n488\t    - LOGO 5-class F1\n489\t    rows:\n490\t    - - XGBoost 7-feature\n491\t      - 0.38\n492\t      - 0.72\n493\t      - 0.34\n494\t    - - QLoRA Qwen3-0.6B\n495\t      - 0.44\n496\t      - 0.76\n497\t      - 0.38\n498\t    - - Delta\n499\t      - '+0.06'\n500\t      - '+0.04'\n501\t      - '+0.04'\n502\t  - name: 'Table: QLoRA LOGO Per-family Held-out'\n503\t    columns:\n504\t    - Held-out Family\n505\t    - 5-class F1\n506\t    - Overfitting gap\n507\t    rows:\n508\t    - - Pythia (2.8B+1B)\n509\t      - 0.52\n510\t      - 0.1\n511\t    - - OLMo-2-1B\n512\t      - 0.35\n513\t      - 0.27\n514\t    - - Qwen (1.7B+0.6B)\n515\t      - 0.38\n516\t      - 0.24\n517\t  figures_description:\n518\t  - 'Fig 7: Learning curves (train/val F1 vs epoch). Val F1 plateaus at epoch 3 while\n519\t    train continues climbing → clear overfitting signal. Val F1 on held-out families\n520\t    (OLMo/Qwen) peaks at epoch 2 then degrades.'\n521\t  analysis: 'E2E model provides modest improvement over handcrafted features but does\n522\t    not solve the fundamental problem: depth signal for non-Pythia architectures is\n523\t    weak or absent. The overfitting pattern (generator-specific memorization) is actually\n524\t    diagnostic evidence for the reframed paper: it shows that whatever distinguishes\n525\t    depths for a given generator is not transferable across architectures. This supports\n526\t    the ''architecture-conditional depth response'' thesis — each model family has\n527\t    its own depth signature (if any), and there is no universal learned representation\n528\t    of ''depth''. For the paper: report as supplementary evidence that neither handcrafted\n529\t    nor learned features achieve universal depth discrimination, strengthening the\n530\t    conditional-claim reframing.'\n531\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6280c30-44d5-4994-84cb-c73cc98d88f7","uuid":"3d4826f9-8ed8-4cde-bba7-e94cccb70135","timestamp":"2026-05-16T16:28:27.395Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_3/projects/gen-depth-fingerprint/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T155725/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 放弃 'universal depth signal' 叙事，转向 'architecture-conditional depth\n  response'。核心贡献变为：识别 depth signal 存在/崩溃的条件，以及 signal 缺失本身作为生成器 fingerprint 的二阶信号。仍冲\n  EMNLP，定位为 negative/characterization paper。\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: feature_ablation_and_trend\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: MVP Pythia-only 数据上的特征消融 + 趋势分析 + perplexity 预验证\n  expected_results:\n    full_macro_f1: 0.81\n    reference_only_f1: 0.68\n    surface_only_f1: 0.77\n    ref_vs_surf_bootstrap_p: 0.003\n    h2_features: entropy_mean (slope=-0.42, R²=0.88), ttr (slope=-0.11, R²=0.91),\n      hapax_ratio (slope=-0.14, R²=0.93)\n    h1_features: tail_decay (slope=-0.02, R²=0.15), entropy_std (slope=+0.01, R²=0.08),\n      entropy_max (slope=-0.06, R²=0.31), entropy_min (slope=-0.09, R²=0.42)\n    entropy_min_ambiguous: true\n    median_ppl_by_depth: 13.2, 5.1, 3.2, 2.3, 1.8\n    ppl_depth_spearman: -0.95\n  result_rationale: Pythia-410M reference + Pythia-2.8B generator 是 same-family 最佳条件，即使在\n    worst 档位下初始 MVP 数据仍然能看到 depth signal。问题不在这里暴露——surface features（TTR/hapax）占主导（0.77\n    vs ref-only 0.68）暗示 depth signal 主要来自 vocabulary impoverishment 而非深层 distributional\n    structure。entropy_min 的 R²=0.42 处于模糊地带（不完全 stationary），为后续 cross-family 失败埋下伏笔：这种\n    intermediate behavior 说明 drifting/stationary 分界在不同架构下可能不一致。Reference features\n    弱于 surface 是 worst 档早期信号——如果 dual dynamics 是 robust phenomenon，reference features\n    应至少持平。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Feature Ablation (5-fold CV, Pythia-2.8B only)'\n    columns:\n    - Feature Set\n    - Macro F1\n    - 95% CI\n    rows:\n    - - Full 7-feature\n      - 0.81\n      - '[0.79, 0.83]'\n    - - Surface only (TTR + hapax)\n      - 0.77\n      - '[0.75, 0.79]'\n    - - Reference only (5 entropy feats)\n      - 0.68\n      - '[0.65, 0.71]'\n    - - entropy_mean alone\n      - 0.64\n      - '[0.61, 0.67]'\n  - name: 'Table: Linear Trend per Feature (depth 0-4)'\n    columns:\n    - Feature\n    - Slope\n    - R²\n    - Classification\n    rows:\n    - - hapax_ratio\n      - -0.14\n      - 0.93\n      - Drifting\n    - - ttr\n      - -0.11\n      - 0.91\n      - Drifting\n    - - entropy_mean\n      - -0.42\n      - 0.88\n      - Drifting\n    - - entropy_min\n      - -0.09\n      - 0.42\n      - Ambiguous\n    - - entropy_max\n      - -0.06\n      - 0.31\n      - Stationary\n    - - tail_decay\n      - -0.02\n      - 0.15\n      - Stationary\n    - - entropy_std\n      - 0.01\n      - 0.08\n      - Stationary\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 1: 7 个特征 mean±std across depth 0-4。hapax/ttr/entropy_mean 呈明显单调下降，entropy_std/tail_decay\n    基本平坦，entropy_min 呈弱下降趋势（R²=0.42），预示跨架构不一致的隐患。'\n  analysis: 'Initial signal looks promising on same-family data but two warning signs:\n    (1) surface features dominate reference features by 9pp, suggesting vocabulary\n    impoverishment is the primary signal carrier, not distributional structure shifts;\n    (2) entropy_min sits in an ambiguous zone. In worst tier these are early indicators\n    that the ''dual dynamics'' framework is architecture-specific — it cleanly separates\n    on Pythia but may not generalize. Proceed to plan_002 but with lowered expectations\n    for cross-family transfer.'\n- name: cross_generator_evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: 5 生成器 (Pythia-2.8B/1B, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-0.6B) LOGO 交叉验证\n  expected_results:\n    total_records: 18200\n    logo_avg_macro_f1_3class: 0.72\n    logo_avg_binary_f1: 0.67\n    logo_per_generator:\n      pythia-2.8b:\n        3class: 0.82\n        binary: 0.78\n      pythia-1b:\n        3class: 0.84\n        binary: 0.8\n      olmo-2-1b:\n        3class: 0.63\n        binary: 0.58\n      qwen3-1.7b:\n        3class: 0.67\n        binary: 0.62\n      qwen3-0.6b:\n        3class: 0.64\n        binary: 0.57\n    per_gen_f1_std: 0.11\n    leave_one_family_out:\n      held_out_pythia: 0.79\n      held_out_olmo: 0.58\n      held_out_qwen: 0.6\n    ablation_full_f1: 0.72\n    ablation_surface_only_f1: 0.7\n    ablation_reference_only_f1: 0.61\n    mcnemar_full_vs_surface_p: 0.12\n    generators_below_060_binary: 2\n    spearman_by_generator:\n      pythia-2.8b:\n        entropy_mean: -0.61\n        ttr: -0.58\n        hapax: -0.63\n      pythia-1b:\n        entropy_mean: -0.55\n        ttr: -0.54\n        hapax: -0.6\n      olmo-2-1b:\n        entropy_mean: -0.22\n        ttr: -0.35\n        hapax: -0.38\n      qwen3-1.7b:\n        entropy_mean: -0.31\n        ttr: -0.4\n        hapax: -0.43\n      qwen3-0.6b:\n        entropy_mean: -0.18\n        ttr: -0.33\n        hapax: -0.36\n    feature_direction_inconsistency: OLMo entropy_mean correlation weakly negative\n      (-0.22) while Pythia strongly negative (-0.61); effect size ratio 2.8x\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档核心假设在此暴露：2+ 新家族 held-out F1 < 0.60。Pythia 家族内 transfer\n    良好（两个 Pythia 模型互相泄露 inductive bias），但 OLMo 和 Qwen 家族 held-out 时 binary F1 掉到 0.57-0.58。原因：(1)\n    OLMo 的 training recipe（Dolma corpus + unique LR schedule）产生不同的 token frequency\n    distribution，导致 Pythia-410M reference model 的 entropy features 对 OLMo 生成文本的 depth\n    drift 不敏感——entropy_mean 的 Spearman 仅 -0.22（vs Pythia -0.61），effect size 缩小 2.8x；(2)\n    Qwen tokenizer 完全不同（byte-level BPE vs Pythia GPT-NeoX tokenizer），surface features（TTR/hapax）的计算基于不同\n    vocabulary space，导致跨家族 surface feature 分布 mismatch；(3) full vs surface-only 差距仅\n    2pp（0.72 vs 0.70），McNemar p=0.12 不显著——7-feature ensemble 在这个场景下不优于简单 surface features，印证\n    ''seven_feat_vs_best_baseline_pp: [0, 2.0]'' 的 worst 预期。per_gen_f1_std = 0.11\n    远高于 ''universal'' 叙事所需的一致性。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: LOGO Cross-Generator Results'\n    columns:\n    - Held-out Generator\n    - 3-class F1\n    - Binary F1\n    - Family\n    rows:\n    - - Pythia-2.8B\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.78\n      - Pythia\n    - - Pythia-1B\n      - 0.84\n      - 0.8\n      - Pythia\n    - - OLMo-2-1B\n      - 0.63\n      - 0.58\n      - OLMo\n    - - Qwen3-1.7B\n      - 0.67\n      - 0.62\n      - Qwen\n    - - Qwen3-0.6B\n      - 0.64\n      - 0.57\n      - Qwen\n    - - '**Average**'\n      - '**0.72**'\n      - '**0.67**'\n      - —\n  - name: 'Table: Feature Ablation (5-gen LOGO)'\n    columns:\n    - Feature Set\n    - Avg LOGO F1\n    - p vs Full\n    rows:\n    - - Full 7-feature\n      - 0.72\n      - —\n    - - Surface only\n      - 0.7\n      - 0.12 (NS)\n    - - Reference only\n      - 0.61\n      - <0.001\n  - name: 'Table: Spearman ρ (entropy_mean vs depth) by Generator'\n    columns:\n    - Generator\n    - ρ\n    - p-value\n    - Effect interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - Pythia-2.8B\n      - -0.61\n      - <0.001\n      - Strong\n    - - Pythia-1B\n      - -0.55\n      - <0.001\n      - Moderate-Strong\n    - - Qwen3-1.7B\n      - -0.31\n      - <0.001\n      - Weak-Moderate\n    - - Qwen3-0.6B\n      - -0.18\n      - <0.001\n      - Weak\n    - - OLMo-2-1B\n      - -0.22\n      - <0.001\n      - Weak\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 2: Per-generator LOGO F1 bar chart with 95% CI error bars. Clear bimodal\n    pattern: Pythia family (0.78-0.80) vs non-Pythia (0.57-0.62). CI bars for OLMo/Qwen\n    overlap with 0.50 random baseline lower bound.'\n  - 'Fig 3: entropy_mean trend lines (depth 0-4) for each generator. Pythia lines\n    steep and parallel; OLMo nearly flat; Qwen shows weak inconsistent slope. Visual\n    evidence of architecture-conditional response.'\n  analysis: 'Universality claim collapses. The 2-tier pattern (Pythia strong, others\n    weak) indicates depth signal is not an intrinsic property of recursive generation\n    but depends on architecture/training-data alignment with the reference model AND\n    possibly on the generator''s own sampling dynamics. Two interpretations: (A) reference\n    model mismatch — Pythia-410M is a poor scorer for non-Pythia text, inflating entropy\n    baseline and suppressing drift measurement; (B) genuine architecture difference\n    — some models produce more uniform token distributions at every depth, compressing\n    the dynamic range for drift detection. Plan_003 (cross-family reference) will\n    disambiguate. If (A), using OLMo/Qwen reference fixes it; if (B), the signal genuinely\n    doesn''t exist for these families. In worst tier, we expect (B) to dominate. Narrative\n    must pivot to conditional claims.'\n- name: paraphrastic_comparison\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: Paraphrasing chains vs continuation chains 直接对比，测试 attractor convergence\n    理论\n  expected_results:\n    paraphrastic_3class_f1: 0.6\n    paraphrastic_binary_f1: 0.53\n    continuation_3class_f1: 0.72\n    continuation_binary_f1: 0.67\n    f1_3class_delta: -0.12\n    spearman_entropy_mean_para: 0.15\n    spearman_entropy_mean_cont: -0.42\n    spearman_ttr_para: 0.31\n    spearman_ttr_cont: -0.48\n    spearman_hapax_para: 0.28\n    spearman_hapax_cont: -0.51\n    cross_transfer_para_to_cont_f1: 0.38\n    cross_transfer_cont_to_para_f1: 0.42\n    depth_retention_para: 0.92\n    depth_retention_cont: 0.83\n    para_attractor_convergence_gen3: true\n    n_paraphrastic: 4800\n    n_continuation: 4600\n  result_rationale: Worst 档下，paraphrastic chains 呈现 attractor convergence 预期行为：entropy_mean\n    Spearman 仅 +0.15（趋于 neutral/轻微 positive，即 paraphrasing 使 perplexity 略微上升后稳定）。但\n    continuation chains 也弱于 expected——在 5-gen pooled data 上 Spearman 仅 -0.42（而非 best\n    档的 -0.65+），因为 non-Pythia generators 拉低了整体 correlation。关键是 sign reversal：paraphrastic\n    正相关 vs continuation 负相关，但 effect size 都不大。Cross-transfer F1 极低（0.38-0.42），说明两种\n    chain 类型的 feature space 几乎不重叠——这在 worst 档是问题而非 feature，因为它意味着 'depth signal' 高度\n    task-specific，不是一个 unified phenomenon。Depth retention 0.92 for para（高于 continuation\n    的 0.83）也 counterintuitive：paraphrasing 保留更多 chains 但 signal 更弱，说明 chain stability\n    ≠ signal strength。Attractor convergence 在 gen-3 后明显——para chains 的 feature 分布停止变化。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Paraphrastic vs Continuation Depth Signal'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Paraphrastic\n    - Continuation\n    - Delta\n    rows:\n    - - 3-class LOGO F1\n      - 0.6\n      - 0.72\n      - -0.12\n    - - Binary LOGO F1\n      - 0.53\n      - 0.67\n      - -0.14\n    - - ρ(entropy_mean, depth)\n      - '+0.15'\n      - '-0.42'\n      - sign reversed\n    - - ρ(TTR, depth)\n      - '+0.31'\n      - '-0.48'\n      - sign reversed\n    - - ρ(hapax, depth)\n      - '+0.28'\n      - '-0.51'\n      - sign reversed\n    - - Depth retention (gen4/gen0)\n      - 0.92\n      - 0.83\n      - '+0.09'\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-transfer LOGO F1'\n    columns:\n    - Train on\n    - Test on\n    - F1\n    rows:\n    - - Continuation\n      - Continuation\n      - 0.72\n    - - Paraphrastic\n      - Paraphrastic\n      - 0.6\n    - - Continuation → Para\n      - Paraphrastic\n      - 0.42\n    - - Para → Continuation\n      - Continuation\n      - 0.38\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 4: Parallel feature trajectories (depth 0-4) for para vs cont chains. Continuation\n    lines drift downward (vocabulary impoverishment); paraphrastic lines converge\n    to plateau by gen-3 (attractor behavior). 但两者 effect sizes 都小于 expected。'\n  analysis: 'Sign reversal confirms theoretically expected behavior (paraphrasing\n    → attractor convergence, continuation → monotonic drift), but under worst tier\n    the effect sizes are underwhelming for both types. Paraphrastic binary F1=0.53\n    is near random — essentially unclassifiable beyond gen-0 vs rest. Continuation\n    is better but still weak (0.67 binary). The low cross-transfer (0.38-0.42) means\n    there''s no unified ''depth signal'' that works across chain types — each requires\n    its own model. For EMNLP reframing: this SUPPORTS the ''architecture-conditional''\n    narrative because it shows depth signal properties depend on the specific generation\n    process (paraphrasing vs continuation vs architecture), not just depth itself.\n    The attractor convergence finding is a positive contribution to theory validation\n    even in worst case.'\n- name: finer_grained_ordinal\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: 5-class ordinal classification (gen-0 through gen-4) 测试更细粒度深度估计\n  expected_results:\n    5class_macro_f1: 0.38\n    5class_f1_std: 0.04\n    5class_accuracy: 0.42\n    5class_mae: 0.95\n    3class_macro_f1: 0.72\n    delta_5class_vs_3class: -0.34\n    per_class_f1:\n      depth_0: 0.85\n      depth_1: 0.45\n      depth_2: 0.22\n      depth_3: 0.18\n      depth_4: 0.2\n    confusion_concentration: gen2/gen3/gen4 互相混淆，占 confusion matrix off-diagonal 的\n      72%\n    ordinal_methods:\n      CORAL: 0.36\n      frank_hall: 0.39\n      xgboost: 0.38\n    depth_2_3_separability: Cohen's d = 0.08 (entropy_mean), 0.12 (hapax_ratio) —\n      几乎不可分\n    per_family_5class:\n      pythia_held_out: 0.48\n      olmo_held_out: 0.28\n      qwen_held_out: 0.31\n  result_rationale: Worst 档下，5-class 在 pooled 5-gen data 上 macro F1 仅 0.38，接近 5-class\n    random baseline（0.20）但仍显著高于 chance。核心问题：depth 2/3/4 几乎不可分（per-class F1 0.18-0.22）。原因是双重的：(1)\n    depth drift 在多数生成器（OLMo/Qwen）上本身就弱，加上 (2) gen-2 到 gen-4 之间的 feature 增量极小（Cohen's\n    d < 0.12），即使在 Pythia 上也进入 plateau。只有 gen-0 可靠分类（F1=0.85），gen-1 中等（0.45）——这本质上是\n    binary detection（gen-0 vs rest）在 5-class 框架中的残影。OLMo/Qwen held-out 时 5-class F1\n    掉到 0.28-0.31（接近 random），进一步说明 fine-grained 深度估计只在特定架构下可行。Ordinal-specific methods（CORAL/Frank-Hall）无优势，因为\n    underlying signal 本身不存在于 deep depths。3-class（0.72）远优于 5-class（0.38），但 delta =\n    34pp 说明 3-class 的性能也主要来自 gen-0 classification 而非真正的 ordinal discrimination。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Ordinal Classification Results'\n    columns:\n    - Granularity\n    - Method\n    - Macro F1\n    - MAE\n    rows:\n    - - 3-class\n      - XGBoost\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.31\n    - - 5-class\n      - XGBoost\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.95\n    - - 5-class\n      - CORAL\n      - 0.36\n      - 0.98\n    - - 5-class\n      - Frank-Hall\n      - 0.39\n      - 0.92\n  - name: 'Table: 5-class Per-depth F1'\n    columns:\n    - Depth\n    - F1\n    - Support\n    - Most confused with\n    rows:\n    - - gen-0\n      - 0.85\n      - 4950\n      - gen-1 (10%)\n    - - gen-1\n      - 0.45\n      - 4900\n      - gen-2 (28%)\n    - - gen-2\n      - 0.22\n      - 4600\n      - gen-3 (35%), gen-1 (22%)\n    - - gen-3\n      - 0.18\n      - 4200\n      - gen-2 (33%), gen-4 (30%)\n    - - gen-4\n      - 0.2\n      - 3800\n      - gen-3 (38%), gen-2 (21%)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 5: 5×5 Confusion matrix heatmap。gen-0 行几乎全在对角线；gen-2/3/4 行呈均匀分布，对角线无明显 peak。直观展示\n    depth > 1 的不可分性。'\n  - 'Fig 6: Feature distributions (violin plots) by depth 0-4, split by generator\n    family。Pythia violins 逐层分离；OLMo/Qwen violins 从 depth-1 开始完全重叠。'\n  analysis: '5-class ordinal is infeasible in worst tier. The signal exists primarily\n    at the gen-0/gen-1 boundary and rapidly degrades. This is actually informative\n    for the reframed paper: it establishes an empirical ceiling on depth resolution\n    (≤3 classes) that''s architecture-dependent. For Pythia-family generators where\n    signal is strong, 4-class might work; for others, even binary (gen-1 vs gen-2+)\n    is near chance. The ''conditions under which depth signal emerges vs collapses''\n    framing gains direct evidence: depth granularity is architecture-conditional,\n    not a universal property of recursive generation. Report as structured negative\n    finding.'\n- name: end_to_end_classifier\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: QLoRA fine-tuned Qwen3.5-0.8B 端到端深度分类，对比 handcrafted features\n  expected_results:\n    5class_macro_f1: 0.44\n    5class_f1_std: 0.02\n    3class_macro_f1: 0.76\n    3class_f1_std: 0.01\n    per_class_f1:\n      gen0: 0.95\n      gen1: 0.62\n      gen2: 0.3\n      gen3: 0.22\n      gen4: 0.11\n    vs_xgboost_5class_delta_pp: '+6.0'\n    vs_xgboost_3class_delta_pp: '+4.0'\n    logo_generalization:\n      pythia_held_out: 0.52\n      olmo_held_out: 0.35\n      qwen_held_out: 0.38\n    overfitting_gap: 0.18\n    train_f1: 0.62\n    val_f1: 0.44\n    runtime_hours: 14\n    model: Qwen3-0.6B-Base\n    method: QLoRA rank-16\n  result_rationale: E2E model 在 5-class 上优于 XGBoost（0.44 vs 0.38，+6pp），因为 learned\n    representations 能捕获 handcrafted features 遗漏的 subtle patterns（如 attention pattern\n    shifts、specific n-gram frequency changes）。但绝对性能仍然很差（0.44），且 overfitting 严重（train\n    0.62 vs val 0.44，gap=18pp）——模型学到了 generator-specific artifacts 而非 generalizable\n    depth signal。LOGO generalization 更加灾难性：held-out Pythia F1=0.52，OLMo/Qwen 仅 0.35-0.38。这说明\n    E2E model 学到的不是 'depth signal' 而是 'generator fingerprint + depth 交互'——它在训练集内的\n    generator 上过拟合。3-class（0.76）优于 XGBoost（0.72）但差距不大（+4pp），且同样来自 gen-0 classification。在\n    worst 档下，E2E 的相对优势说明确实有 beyond-handcrafted-features 的信号存在，但这些信号 generator-specific、不泛化，支持\n    'architecture-conditional' reframing。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: E2E vs Handcrafted Features'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - 5-class F1\n    - 3-class F1\n    - LOGO 5-class F1\n    rows:\n    - - XGBoost 7-feature\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.34\n    - - QLoRA Qwen3-0.6B\n      - 0.44\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.38\n    - - Delta\n      - '+0.06'\n      - '+0.04'\n      - '+0.04'\n  - name: 'Table: QLoRA LOGO Per-family Held-out'\n    columns:\n    - Held-out Family\n    - 5-class F1\n    - Overfitting gap\n    rows:\n    - - Pythia (2.8B+1B)\n      - 0.52\n      - 0.1\n    - - OLMo-2-1B\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.27\n    - - Qwen (1.7B+0.6B)\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.24\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 7: Learning curves (train/val F1 vs epoch). Val F1 plateaus at epoch 3 while\n    train continues climbing → clear overfitting signal. Val F1 on held-out families\n    (OLMo/Qwen) peaks at epoch 2 then degrades.'\n  analysis: 'E2E model provides modest improvement over handcrafted features but does\n    not solve the fundamental problem: depth signal for non-Pythia architectures is\n    weak or absent. The overfitting pattern (generator-specific memorization) is actually\n    diagnostic evidence for the reframed paper: it shows that whatever distinguishes\n    depths for a given generator is not transferable across architectures. This supports\n    the ''architecture-conditional depth response'' thesis — each model family has\n    its own depth signature (if any), and there is no universal learned representation\n    of ''depth''. For the paper: report as supplementary evidence that neither handcrafted\n    nor learned features achieve universal depth discrimination, strengthening the\n    conditional-claim reframing.'\n","numLines":531,"startLine":1,"totalLines":531}}}
