{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NZa8RWPEh4WXZHpsS7vgPB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tTable~\\ref{tab:confusion} reports the aggregated confusion matrix from 6-generator leave-one-generator-out (LOGO) evaluation, collapsed to three ordinal classes: gen-0 (human), gen-1 (first-generation), and gen-2+ (depth $\\geq$ 2).\n2\t\n3\t\\begin{table}[h]\n4\t\\centering\n5\t\\small\n6\t\\begin{tabular}{lccc}\n7\t\\toprule\n8\t& \\textbf{Pred gen-0} & \\textbf{Pred gen-1} & \\textbf{Pred gen-2+} \\\\\n9\t\\midrule\n10\t\\textbf{True gen-0} & 5{,}937 (99.4\\%) & 35 (0.6\\%) & 0 (0.0\\%) \\\\\n11\t\\textbf{True gen-1} & 368 (6.2\\%) & 4{,}437 (75.0\\%) & 1{,}113 (18.8\\%) \\\\\n12\t\\textbf{True gen-2+} & 464 (3.0\\%) & 3{,}646 (23.3\\%) & 11{,}529 (73.7\\%) \\\\\n13\t\\bottomrule\n14\t\\end{tabular}\n15\t\\caption{Aggregated confusion matrix ($N=27{,}529$). Each cell shows count and row-normalized percentage. Gen-0 is near-perfectly identified. Gen-1 errors are asymmetric: misclassification as gen-2+ (18.8\\%) is 3$\\times$ more frequent than as gen-0 (6.2\\%), indicating that gen-1 text already carries detectable recursive distortion. (6-generator LOGO; 3-class: gen-0/gen-1/gen-2+.)}\n16\t\\label{tab:confusion}\n17\t\\end{table}\n18\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LzAvbmoKXc5vyT8aamp4a2","session_id":"c6280c30-44d5-4994-84cb-c73cc98d88f7","uuid":"0cc14cff-eadc-497c-9b03-b83450c26726","timestamp":"2026-05-16T16:30:21.274Z"}
