{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D1NFNkdwYgw37273aaWKfh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\section*{Ethics Statement}\n2\t\\label{sec:ethics}\n3\t\n4\tAll texts analyzed in this work are LLM-generated from publicly available Wikipedia seeds; no personal or sensitive data is involved.\n5\tOur method estimates the generation depth of a text passage---how many recursive generation steps it has undergone---not the identity of its author.\n6\tIndividual authorship attribution is outside both the scope and the capability of this approach; privacy implications are minimal.\n7\tWe acknowledge that depth estimation tools could in principle be used to selectively suppress machine-generated text in contexts where such content is legitimate (e.g., accessibility tools, assistive writing).\n8\tWe encourage deployment in data governance pipelines where provenance transparency---rather than content removal---is the objective.\n9\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LzAvbmoKXc5vyT8aamp4a2","session_id":"c6280c30-44d5-4994-84cb-c73cc98d88f7","uuid":"6a87adc6-631c-455a-87cd-4dd117738f8c","timestamp":"2026-05-16T16:30:22.415Z"}
